---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Install" description="Install daily from source with Python, Rust, and maturin." current="install">
  <section class="shell page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
    <h1>Up and running in a minute.</h1>
    <p>`daily` is currently installed from the source checkout. Build the Rust extension into your active Python environment with maturin.</p>
  </section>
  <article class="shell article">
    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul><li>Python 3.10 or newer</li><li>Rust and Cargo</li><li>Node.js is only needed to work on this website</li></ul>
    <h2>Build and install locally</h2>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/cotanjant/daily.git
cd daily
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install maturin
maturin develop</code></pre>
    <p>On Windows PowerShell, activate the environment with <code>.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1</code>. The package imports as <code>daily</code>.</p>
    <h2>Build a wheel</h2>
    <pre><code>maturin build --release
python -m pip install target/wheels/&lt;wheel-name&gt;.whl</code></pre>
    <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/cotanjant/daily/blob/main/docs/usage.md">usage guide</a> for the available functions.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
